
========== Metadatos del servidor de autorizacion ==========
El issuer es el nombre interno de la red, no localhost: es la direccion con
la que los microservicios alcanzan al auth-server para bajar la clave
publica. El token pedido desde el host por el puerto publicado lleva ese
mismo issuer, asi que los Resource Servers lo validan sin aflojar la
comprobacion.
$ curl http://localhost:9000/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
{"issuer":"http://auth-server:9000","authorization_endpoint":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/authorize","device_authorization_endpoint":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/device_authorization","token_endpoint":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/token","token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported":["client_secret_basic","client_secret_post","client_secret_jwt","private_key_jwt","tls_client_auth","self_signed_tls_client_auth"],"jwks_uri":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/jwks","response_types_supported":["code"],"grant_types_supported":["authorization_code","client_credentials","refresh_token","urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code","urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange"],"revocation_endpoint":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/revoke","revocation_endpoint_auth_methods_supported":["client_secret_basic","client_secret_post","client_secret_jwt","private_key_jwt","tls_client_auth","self_signed_tls_client_auth"],"introspection_endpoint":"http://auth-server:9000/oauth2/introspect","introspection_endpoint_auth_methods_supported":["client_secret_basic","client_secret_post","client_secret_jwt","private_key_jwt","tls_client_auth","self_signed_tls_client_auth"],"code_challenge_methods_supported":["S256"],"tls_client_certificate_bound_access_tokens":true}

